[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4701421510","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120281#issuecomment-4701421510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120281","id":4701421510,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGDn_xg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-14T10:09:24Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T10:09:24Z","body":"> RichTextLabel's size aware images can have images in the wrong position if the font size changes size in the same line.\nIt seems to use the biggest font size in the line as reference, so the smaller line images are put way above the text.\n\nNot a bug, alignment is relative to the whole line, not specific span of the text, and default is center-center, so this is expected. But I guess with addition of font specific sizing it might sense to allow aligning it to the span instead:\n\n<img width=\"596\" height=\"104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/57a2ab84-cf58-4dd0-8651-5142a2e1aba3\" />\n\n> Manually changing the alignment also does not seems to be working, producing unexpected results or none at all.\n\nThis seems to be a bug, not related to the font-size specific sizing, it is the same if sizes are set manually (and behavior is the same at least since 4.5).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4701421510/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4701462204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120281#issuecomment-4701462204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120281","id":4701462204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGDqevA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-14T10:27:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T10:27:18Z","body":"The second one is a limitation of BBcode, you can't use both `img=` with `height=` in the same tag, it's either only `img=align` or `img align=top,bottom height=x` if you want to use multiple arguments.\n\nBoth 